===== path p derive
Derive a Toolpath document from a source and stream it to stdout (the stdout-only sibling of `import`; equivalent to `import … --no-cache`)

Usage: path p derive [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  git       Import from git repository history
  github    Import from a GitHub pull request
  claude    Import from Claude conversation logs
  gemini    Import from Gemini CLI conversation logs
  codex     Import from Codex CLI rollout files
  copilot   Import from GitHub Copilot CLI session logs (preview)
  opencode  Import from opencode session databases
  cursor    Import from Cursor (IDE) composers in `state.vscdb`
  pi        Import from Pi (pi.dev) coding-agent session logs
  pathbase  Import from Pathbase (download a previously uploaded path)
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
===== path p derive claude
Import from Claude conversation logs

Usage: path p derive claude [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -p, --project <PROJECT>
          Project path (omit to interactively pick across all projects)

  -s, --session <SESSION>
          Specific session ID (omit to interactively pick)

      --all
          Process all sessions in the project

      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
===== path p derive codex
Import from Codex CLI rollout files

Usage: path p derive codex [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -s, --session <SESSION>
          Session id, UUID, or filename stem (default: most recent)

      --all
          Process all sessions (emits one Path per session)

      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
