===== path p derive git
Import from git repository history

Usage: path p derive git [OPTIONS] --branch <BRANCH>

Options:
  -r, --repo <REPO>
          Path to the git repository
          
          [default: .]

  -b, --branch <BRANCH>
          Branch name(s). Format: `name` or `name:start`

      --base <BASE>
          Global base commit (overrides per-branch starts)

      --remote <REMOTE>
          Remote name for URI generation
          
          [default: origin]

      --title <TITLE>
          Graph title (for multi-branch output)

      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
===== path p derive github
Import from a GitHub pull request

Usage: path p derive github [OPTIONS] [URL]

Arguments:
  [URL]
          PR URL (e.g. <https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/42>)

Options:
  -r, --repo <REPO>
          Repository in owner/repo format (alternative to URL)

      --pr <PR>
          Pull request number (required with --repo)

      --no-ci
          Exclude CI check runs

      --no-comments
          Exclude reviews and comments

      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
===== path p derive opencode
Import from opencode session databases

Usage: path p derive opencode [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -s, --session <SESSION>
          Session id (default: most recent)

      --all
          Process all sessions (emits one Path per session)

      --project <PROJECT>
          Filter by project id (SHA of repo's first root commit)

      --no-snapshot-diffs
          Skip snapshot-based file diff extraction

      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

